    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling lineup led by **James Wood** (76.27) and **Brice Turang** (75.05). **James Wood** is our standout play; his 0.401 xwOBA combined with a favorable matchup against Kelly (xERA 4.74) and a stolen base efficiency bump against a slower delivery creates an elite environment for production. Similarly, **Brice Turang** benefits from a strong park factor and a soft matchup against Feltner, making him the anchor of our middle-infield production. **Seiya Suzuki** (68.60) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (62.26) also maintain strong profiles, providing the necessary volume to challenge in HR and RBI categories without sacrificing the efficiency required to maintain our season-long pacing.\n\nThe rotation decision for our final spots was tight, specifically regarding **Zach McKinstry** (38.67), who narrowly missed the cut. While **Zach McKinstry** offered potential, his projected SP skill disadvantage against Woo forced him below our 40.0 floor, prioritizing the upside of **Josh Naylor** (61.00) even against a tough arm in Valdez. We are monitoring **Corbin Carroll** closely; despite a respectable 60.87 score, the combination of a difficult arm in Griffin and the presence of an elite catcher (1.89s pop time) suppresses his stolen base upside. If late-breaking weather reports or lineup shuffling shift the leverage, we have depth ready, though players like **Jose Caballero** remain sidelined today. With **Trevor Story** and **Mickey Moniak** still on the IL, we must maximize the output from **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Travis Bazzana**, **Austin Riley**, **Carson Williams**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Kyle Karros**, **Alex Freeland**, **Henry Bolte**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, and **Max Muncy** to keep pace in this competitive Roto landscape.",
